                                   Palm oil is a potential agricultural product in Indonesia, particularly in improving the
ICSAFS Conference                  economy of the country. Indonesia produced 17.5 million tons crude palm oil (CPO) in
Committee.                         2008 which increased up to24.4 million tons in 2013 with a productivity of 3600 kg/ha
                                   [1]. The world’s high demand for CPO is utilized in the food industry for cooking oil,
                                   margarine and emulsiﬁers, cosmetics, detergents, as well as for the energy industry
                                   as a raw material for biodiesel and bioethanol production.
                                      Along with the increase of oil palm cultivation and the processing of palm oil, the
                                   CPO industry also produces various wastes, respectively the stem, stem leaf, husk,

How to cite this article: Efri Mardawati, Dwi Wahyudha Wira, M. Djali, Fetriyuna, and Edi Suryadi, (2017), “Optimization and Kinetic Modelling of The
Enzymatic Hydrolysis of Oil Palm Petioles” in 2nd International Conference on Sustainable Agriculture and Food Security: A Comprehensive Approach, Page 439
